        <mxCell id="s1-note" parent="1" style="shape=note;size=14;fillColor=#e0e0e0;strokeColor=#9e9e9e;fontSize=9;align=left;spacingLeft=5;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap" value="SECTION 1 DATA FLOW:&#xa;1. Orchestrator reads pom.xml / build.gradle, resolves dependencies&#xa;2. javac compiles each .java → .class (bytecode)&#xa;3. jar packages .class files + resources into .jar archive&#xa;4. Dependencies fetched from Maven Central (not embedded)&#xa;&#xa;Key: Java has no linker step — JARs are just ZIP archives&#xa;Dependencies resolved at runtime via classpath, not embedded&#xa;&#xa;Top Java Build Orchestrators:&#xa;• Maven — XML-based (pom.xml), most common&#xa;• Gradle — Groovy/Kotlin DSL, Android default&#xa;• Ant — XML-based, legacy&#xa;• SBT — Scala projects&#xa;• Bazel — Google&#39;s polyglot build system" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="195" width="280" x="687" y="95" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="div1" parent="1" style="line;strokeWidth=3;strokeColor=#111111;dashed=1" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="10" width="980" x="40" y="318" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
